+/* The x86/x64 implementation above keeps the query profile in a striped lane
+ * layout and propagates the F (insertion) term with the SWPS3 lazy-F block.
+ * Neither is available off x86, so the same recurrences are evaluated cell by
+ * cell here, with a linear profile layout and F propagated directly:
+ *   H(i,j)   = max{H(i-1,j-1)+S(i,j), E(i,j), F(i,j)}
+ *   E(i+1,j) = max{H(i,j)-gapo, E(i,j)-gape}
+ *   F(i,j+1) = max{H(i,j)-gapo, F(i,j)-gape}
+ * The KSW_ADDS_* and KSW_SUBS_* helpers below mirror _mm_adds_epu8,
+ * _mm_subs_epu8, _mm_adds_epi16 and _mm_subs_epu16, so scores saturate
+ * exactly as they do on the SIMD path. */
